Chapter: MicPeakTest
  cites Kernel chapter HdaAudio

 The microphone loudness analysis (hda-peak), checked on a synthetic PCM
 buffer -- deterministic and silent, so it runs in the battery without a
 microphone. hda-peak reads the left channel of each stereo frame (bytes
 0,1 of every 4) as a signed 16-bit little-endian sample and returns the
 largest absolute value. The buffer below puts +100 in frame 0 and -5000
 in frame 1 (0xEC78 little-endian: 120, 236) and leaves the rest zero, so
 the peak is 5000.

Section: Body

  check : Integer -> Text
  check (x) =
    let buf = alloc-bytes 32
    in let w0 = poke-byte buf 0 100
    in let w1 = poke-byte buf 1 0
    in let w2 = poke-byte buf 4 120
    in let w3 = poke-byte buf 5 236
    in let p = hda-peak buf 8
    in if p == 5000 then "PASS" else "FAIL: peak = " & show p

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (check 0)
  end
